{"Title":"An Act relative to a clean transportation future","BillNumber":"H3182","DocketNumber":"HD965","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"PJK1","Name":"Patrick Joseph Kearney","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PJK1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T17:12:17.597"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"PJK1","Name":"Patrick Joseph Kearney","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PJK1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-17T17:12:17.5966667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3182/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Kearney of Scituate, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3182) of Patrick Joseph Kearney relative to promoting zero-emission vehicles.  Telecommunications, Utilities and Energy.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1: Section 2 of Chapter 90 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting in line 448 after the words, “thereunder.” the following:\r\n\tOn and after January 1, 2038, the registrar shall not accept an application for original registration for any motor vehicle unless that vehicle is a zero emissions vehicle. For the purposes of this section, “zero emissions vehicle” means a vehicle that produces zero exhaust emissions of any criteria pollutant or precursor pollutant, or greenhouse gas, excluding emissions from air conditioning systems, under any and all possible operating modes or conditions.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J37","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J37"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}